creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0161205Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0169739Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0254793Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0263053Z ^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0263408Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0263850Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0264096Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0264322Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0265287Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0265626Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0265856Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0266449Z    if you are ready to continue.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0266761Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0267243Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0268561Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0269062Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0269467Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0269639Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0269770Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0269966Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0270121Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0270417Z    can use Nix.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0270549Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0270625Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0270757Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0270986Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0271342Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0278097Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0278616Z I will:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0278817Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0279023Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0279467Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0279816Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0280212Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0280525Z  - install Nix in /nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0280831Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0281289Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0281732Z    /root
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0289015Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0289726Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0298841Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0299654Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0300342Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0300707Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0301220Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0316619Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0317101Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0326216Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0326859Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0327392Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0327778Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0327951Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0328227Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0328476Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0329043Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0329276Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0329386Z If you would like to
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0329680Z see the output, try like this:
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0329897Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0330095Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0330521Z   $ sh ./install-nix
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0330688Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0331094Z 
creation	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:50.0332144Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
