archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1613274Z Note: a multi-user installation is possible. See https://nix.dev/manual/nix/stable/installation/installing-binary.html#multi-user-installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1621853Z ^[[1;31mSwitching to the Multi-user Installer^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1704644Z ^[[32mWelcome to the Multi-User Nix Installation
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1712328Z ^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1713004Z This installation tool will set up your computer with the Nix package
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1713937Z manager. This will happen in a few stages:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1714421Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1714909Z 1. Make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix. If it does, I
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1716599Z    will show you instructions on how to clean up your old install.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1717067Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1717407Z 2. Show you what I am going to install and where. Then I will ask
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1718118Z    if you are ready to continue.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1718469Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1719168Z 3. Create the system users ^[[34m(uids [30001..30008])^[[0m and groups ^[[34m(gid 30000)^[[0m
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1720151Z    that the Nix daemon uses to run builds. To create system users
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1720984Z    in a different range, exit and run this tool again with
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1721629Z    NIX_FIRST_BUILD_UID set.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1721947Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1722324Z 4. Perform the basic installation of the Nix files daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1722783Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1723018Z 5. Configure your shell to import special Nix Profile files, so you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1723413Z    can use Nix.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1723556Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1723683Z 6. Start the Nix daemon.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1723875Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1724170Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mWould you like to see a more detailed list of what I will do?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1724715Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1725079Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1725620Z I will:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1726137Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1726503Z  - make sure your computer doesn't already have Nix files
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1726936Z    (if it does, I will tell you how to clean them up.)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1727392Z  - create local users (see the list above for the users I'll make)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1727802Z  - create a local group (nixbld)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1728102Z  - install Nix in /nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1728416Z  - create a configuration file in /etc/nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1728834Z  - set up the "default profile" by creating some Nix-related files in
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1729235Z    /root
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1737634Z  - back up /etc/bash.bashrc to /etc/bash.bashrc.backup-before-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1738561Z  - update /etc/bash.bashrc to include some Nix configuration
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1747115Z  - load and start a service (at /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.service
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1747983Z    and /etc/systemd/system/nix-daemon.socket) for nix-daemon
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1748744Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1749158Z ^[[32m^[[4;32mReady to continue?
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1749726Z ^[[0mNo TTY, assuming you would say yes :)
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1763166Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1763876Z ^[[34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1772558Z ^[[0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1773297Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1773882Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1774243Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1774490Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1774760Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1775023Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1775651Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1776121Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1776262Z If you would like to
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1776551Z see the output, try like this:
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1776756Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1776966Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1777355Z   $ sh ./install-nix
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1777508Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1777517Z 
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1777754Z ^[[32m~~> Checking for artifacts of previous installs
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1782657Z ^[[0mBefore I try to install, I'll check for signs Nix already is or has
archive	Run cachix/install-nix-action@v31.11.2	2026-10-19T14:53:53.1783088Z been installed on this system.
